-- A derived-context query made from INSIDE the method it depends on
-- runs a fresh fixpoint (checker-v2.md §11.2): `W`'s `eq` needs `T`'s `key`
-- (through `H.eq`'s `where a.key`), and `key`'s own body compares `W`s. The
-- program's one real error is `other = (T 1).key "s"`: `key : T, () -> Int`,
-- so it is one `type_mismatch` at `"s"`. The twin
-- `DerivedContextReentrantSameFirst/` writes `same` first
-- and must say the same. NOT EQUATABLE `W` would be
-- the right verdict for the wrong reason.
pub type Holder a
    = Holder a


pub eq : Holder a, Holder a → Bool
    where a.key : a, ⊤ → Int
eq left right =
    case left of
        Holder l →
            case right of
                Holder r →
                    l.key ⊤ == r.key ⊤
